intervalIntegral.integral_hasDerivWithin.comment:
Fundamental theorem of calculus: if `f : ℝ → E` is integrable on `a..b` and `f x` is continuous
from the left or from the right at `b`, then `u ↦ ∫ x in a..u, f x` has left (resp., right)
derivative `f b` at `b`.

interval_integral.integral_has_deriv_wit.comment:
Fundamental theorem of calculus: if `f : ℝ → E` is integrable on `a..b` and `f x` is continuous
from the left or from the right at `b`, then `u ↦ ∫ x in a..u, f x` has left (resp., right)
derivative `f b` at `b`.

intervalIntegral.integral_hasDerivWithin.comment:
Fundamental theorem of calculus: if `f : ℝ → E` is integrable on `a..b` and `f x` is continuous
from the left or from the right at `a`, then `u ↦ ∫ x in u..b, f x` has left (resp., right)
derivative `-f a` at `a`.

interval_integral.integral_has_deriv_wit.comment:
Fundamental theorem of calculus: if `f : ℝ → E` is integrable on `a..b` and `f x` is continuous
from the left or from the right at `a`, then `u ↦ ∫ x in u..b, f x` has left (resp., right)
derivative `-f a` at `a`.

